  "reasons": [
    "Gartner sees wafer fab equipment revenue up 29.4% in 2026 and SEMI [chip-equipment trade group] sees 300mm investment up double digits through 2029, which leads to more inspection tools bought per fab.",
    "Shares fell 21% in four weeks because of sector risk-off, not estimates: Morgan Stanley raised 2027 revenue to $21.4B from $20.4B, so a December guide above $4.0B closes the gap.",
    "Net income grew 18.9% to $4.83B on revenue up 11.7% to $13.58B, so each extra tool sold carries more profit \u2014 the leverage the 2027 capex ramp extends."
  ],
  "watch": [
    "December-quarter revenue guide: above $4.0B confirms the capex ramp is reaching KLA; the low end of its own $4.0B \u00b1$200M range breaks it.",
    "EPS against the $1.18 consensus (range $1.15-$1.25): a fifth straight beat confirms; $1.15 or below breaks.",
    "Gross margin: holding the June quarter's $2.24B gross profit on $3.66B revenue confirms pricing; any compression breaks it."
  ],
